@startuml HomeShield FSM - Face / Intruder Detection
title HomeShield - Finite-State Machine (FSM) for Face and Intruder Detection\nArcFace embedding + cosine match; thresholds from homeshield/face.py + settings.py

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
    BorderColor     #92400E
    BackgroundColor<<idle>>    #DCFCE7
    BorderColor<<idle>>        #166534
    BackgroundColor<<inspect>> #DBEAFE
    BorderColor<<inspect>>     #1E40AF
    BackgroundColor<<known>>   #BBF7D0
    BorderColor<<known>>       #166534
    BackgroundColor<<alert>>   #FECACA
    BorderColor<<alert>>       #991B1B
    BackgroundColor<<cool>>    #FEF3C7
    BorderColor<<cool>>        #92400E
    FontName Inter
}

skinparam ArrowColor #1E40AF

[*] --> DISABLED

state "DISABLED" as DISABLED <<idle>> {
    DISABLED : face_enabled = False
    DISABLED : InsightFace engine unloaded.
    DISABLED : (recommended on CPU-only)
}

state "IDLE" as IDLE <<idle>> {
    IDLE : face_enabled = True
    IDLE : Waiting for next slot
    IDLE : frame_idx % face_every_n != 0
}

state "DETECTING" as DET <<inspect>> {
    DET : FaceWorker.submit(frame)
    DET : (non-blocking; runs on
    DET : a separate daemon thread)
    DET : InsightFace .get(frame) ->
    DET : list of {bbox, embedding}
}

state "MATCHING" as MATCH <<inspect>> {
    MATCH : best_match(query, gallery)
    MATCH : cosine similarity vs
    MATCH : PersonStore embeddings
    MATCH : threshold = 0.42\n(face_match_threshold)
}

state "KNOWN_FACE" as KNOWN <<known>> {
    KNOWN : Match score >= 0.42
    KNOWN : person_category =\nadult / child / elderly
    KNOWN : NO alert raised
    KNOWN : Label drawn on overlay
}

state "INTRUDER_PENDING" as PENDING <<inspect>> {
    PENDING : Match score < 0.42
    PENDING : (no entry in gallery)
}

state "INTRUDER_ALERT" as ALERT <<alert>> {
    ALERT : entry / emit Event(intruder_detected)
    ALERT : IntruderStore.add(\n  embedding, snapshot,\n  camera_id, camera_name)
    ALERT : SSE pushed to dashboard
}

state "COOLDOWN (per camera)" as COOL <<cool>> {
    COOL : Same camera will NOT raise
    COOL : another intruder alert for
    COOL : intruder_cooldown = 30 seconds
    COOL : (avoids spam from continuous
    COOL : presence of the same stranger)
}

' ====== Transitions ======

DISABLED --> IDLE          : user toggles face_enabled = True\n(hot reload)
IDLE     --> DISABLED      : user toggles face_enabled = False

IDLE     --> DET           : frame_idx % face_every_n == 0\n(face_every_n = 5)
DET      --> IDLE          : no face in frame\n(empty list)

DET      --> MATCH         : at least one face\nwith embedding

MATCH    --> KNOWN         : best score >= 0.42
MATCH    --> PENDING       : best score < 0.42
KNOWN    --> IDLE          : annotate frame and return

PENDING  --> ALERT         : camera cooldown elapsed
PENDING  --> IDLE          : cooldown not elapsed\n(suppress, but still draw box)

ALERT    --> COOL          : record _intruder_emitted[cam] = ts
COOL     --> IDLE          : 30 seconds elapsed\nfor this camera

note right of DET
  Async by design:
  FaceWorker runs InsightFace on
  its OWN daemon thread, so the
  slow ArcFace pass never stalls
  the pose detector.
  The main pipeline reads
  latest_faces() and uses whatever
  the worker has produced.
end note

note bottom of MATCH
  Cosine similarity over 512-d
  unit-normalised ArcFace vectors.
  Implementation: best_match() in
  homeshield/face.py:
    sims = gallery @ unit(query)
    idx  = argmax(sims)
  Vectorised: one matrix-vector
  multiply per face, fast even for
  a gallery of 20+ family members.
end note

note left of DISABLED
  Settings keys involved
  (homeshield/settings.py):
    face_enabled          = True
    face_match_threshold  = 0.45
      (default in settings; the
       engine default 0.42 wins
       when stricter)
    face_every_n          = 5
    intruder_cooldown     = 30
end note

note right of KNOWN
  KNOWN_FACE is the "happy path".
  The person_category attribute is
  used downstream to decide whether
  a person is treated as a "child"
  for danger-zone alerts.
end note

@enduml
